  "source": "typedesc_arguments_output_type.bal",
  "description": "A call whose output type is inferred from one typedesc parameter (targetType) while another (rowTypes) is only an input: each rowTypes element opens in the type editor for a type (closed record, open record, union of records) and in the expression mode for a typedesc variable or typeof; targetType stays the type-inferring parameter, given or not; and the node's own type field keeps the call's output type, not a row type",
